  "notes": "The single mass equation  \u03c1_K^codata - \u03c1_K^LO = (1/|tr_M|) \u03a3_\u03bb y_\u03bb \u03c7^\u03bb \u0394_\u03bb  is **underdetermined**: 11 unknowns (\u0394_\u03bb for \u03bb \u22a2 6), 1 constraint.  This proof-of-concept assumes singleton support for \u0394_\u03bb and reports (a) the Occam's-razor pick (minimum |\u0394|), and (b) the balanced-partition heuristic (3,2,1).  Both reproduce M(D) exactly by construction.  The categorical question \u2014 *which* \u03bb carries the binding, and why \u2014 is the open P3' problem.  Likely resolution paths: (i) Plancherel-truncation bound MAE(k) \u2264 C\u2080\u00b7[2]_q^{-2(k-3)} via k_max = 12; (ii) jet-knot Hochschild-cohomology obstruction selecting a privileged Wedderburn block; (iii) variational principle minimising \u03a3_\u03bb |\u0394_\u03bb|\u00b2 subject to the mass constraint (Tikhonov / minimum-norm solution = Moore-Penrose pseudoinverse).",
